Here is the revised function that replaces non-ASCII characters before lowercasing, preventing Unicode case foldings (such as U+212A KELVIN SIGN lowercasing to 'k') from introducing ASCII letters:

```python
import re

def slugify(title: str) -> str:
    return re.sub(r'[^A-Za-z0-9]+', '-', title).lower().strip('-')
```

